{
  "title": "Numerical gradient",
  "function": "numerical_gradient",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "f",
      "type": "fnv"
    },
    {
      "name": "x",
      "type": "vec"
    },
    {
      "name": "h",
      "type": "float"
    }
  ],
  "returns": "vec",
  "library": true,
  "hints": [
    "A partial derivative is an ordinary derivative along one axis, with every other coordinate held fixed.",
    "For each i: make a copy of x with x[i] increased by h, another with x[i] decreased by h, and take the central difference of f at those two points.",
    "Don't modify the caller's x. Work on copies (Python: list(x), Rust: x.to_vec(), C++: copy the vector)."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        {
          "fn": "bowl"
        },
        [
          0,
          0
        ],
        1e-05
      ],
      "description": "the bowl slopes down toward (1, −2)",
      "expected": [
        -2.0000000000131024,
        8.00000000005241
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        {
          "fn": "sum_squares"
        },
        [
          1,
          2,
          3
        ],
        1e-05
      ],
      "description": "the gradient of Σxᵢ² is 2x",
      "expected": [
        2.0000000000131024,
        4.000000000026205,
        6.000000000039306
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        {
          "fn": "rosenbrock"
        },
        [
          1,
          1
        ],
        1e-05
      ],
      "description": "(1, 1) is the bottom of the Rosenbrock valley",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        4.000004782974596e-08,
        1.1102252745564225e-14
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        {
          "fn": "mixed"
        },
        [
          2,
          3,
          0
        ],
        1e-05
      ],
      "description": "a function of three variables",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        3.000000000064062,
        2.0000000000131024,
        0.9999999999621422
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        {
          "fn": "linear"
        },
        [
          5,
          -2,
          7
        ],
        1e-05
      ],
      "description": "a linear function has a constant gradient",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        1.9999999999242843,
        -3.0000000002416978,
        0.5000000001587068
      ]
    }
  ]
}
